      <elementaryExchange id="bcb01c0c-9caa-55ec-87db-ba20159bfbe5" amount="0.00352" unitId="db3b2def-24b3-5d7e-a8b7-14695362b285" unitContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" elementaryExchangeId="fc1c42ce-a759-49fa-b987-f1ec5e503db1">
        <name xml:lang="en">Water, cooling, unspecified natural origin</name>
        <unitName xml:lang="en">cubic meter</unitName>
        <comment xml:lang="en">Full flow name: Water, cooling, unspecified natural origin
(2,2,5,1,3,na)
, 
Calculated based on literature, (Vionnet, S., Quantis Water Database - Technical Report, 2012). Assumed to have the same data as for anode, aluminium electrolysis / GLO. The process starts with unloading of process materials to their storage areas on site. It includes the processes: recovery of spent anode materials, anode mix preparation, anode block or briquette forming and baking, rodding of baked anodes, maintenance and repair of plant and equipment and treatment of process air, liquids and solids. The process ends when the output (rodded anodes or briquettes) is ready to be transported to an electrolysis plant (primary aluminium smelter). It is assumed that only the total water use is reported and that 80% is used as cooling water and 20% is used as process water.

BAFU mapping audit: {"bafu source exchange index": 27}</comment>
        <uncertainty>
          <lognormal meanValue="0.00352" varianceWithPedigreeUncertainty="0.058705488994996946" mu="-5.649294289372131"/>
